---
import { Fragment } from 'astro/jsx-runtime';
// The returns policy, and a deliberate decision inside it.
//
// Made-to-order goods can be exempt from the 14-day cancellation right in
// the Consumer Contracts Regulations 2013, and a shop printing to order
// could argue that exemption. This one does not. It offers 30 days from
// delivery, no reason needed.
//
// Partly because it sells more. Mostly because the alternative - a shop
// with no returns, selling on Google, on a brand-new domain - is the exact
// profile Merchant Center reviewers are trained to be suspicious of, and
// "denying return and refund for a product despite having a clear refund or
// return policy" is an egregious violation with no warning stage. A policy
// generous enough to honour without argument is cheaper than an appeal.
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { B, money } from '../lib/shop';
import { edge, TTL_STATIC } from '../lib/cache';
const customerPays = B.returns.who_pays_return_postage === 'customer';
edge(Astro.response, TTL_STATIC);
---

<Base
  title="Returns and refunds"
  description={`${B.returns.window_days} days to return anything from the day it arrives, for any reason. Refunds go back to your original payment method within 5 working days of the parcel reaching us.`}
>
  <div class="wrap page narrow">
    <h1>Returns and refunds</h1>

    <p class="prose">
      <strong>{B.returns.window_days} days from the day it arrives, for any
      reason.</strong> You do not have to tell us why. If you have changed
      your mind, if the colour is not what you pictured, if it does not suit
      the wall — send it back.
    </p>

    <h2>How to do it</h2>
    <ol class="prose">
      <li>Email <a href={`mailto:${B.email}`}>{B.email}</a> with your order
        number and say what you are sending back.</li>
      <li>We reply with the return address, usually the same working day.</li>
      <li>Post it back in packaging that will protect the glazing. The
        board it arrived in is ideal.</li>
      <li>We refund within 5 working days of the parcel reaching us.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>What it costs you</h2>
    <table class="plain">
      <tr>
        <th>Return postage</th>
        <td>
          {customerPays
            ? 'Paid by you, unless the item is faulty, damaged or not what you ordered — then we pay.'
            : 'We pay. We will send you a prepaid label.'}
        </td>
      </tr>
      <tr><th>Restocking fee</th><td>{B.returns.restocking_fee === 0 ? 'None. We do not charge one.' : money(B.returns.restocking_fee)}</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Original delivery charge</th><td>Refunded in full if you return the whole order.</td></tr>
      <tr><th>Refund method</th><td>Back to the card or account you paid with. We cannot refund to anything else.</td></tr>
    </table>

    {/* EXCHANGES, stated because we offer them and Merchant Center asks.
        The order matters: the box in Merchant Center is only honest once
        the published policy says this, and the policy URL is what Google
        reads during verification. */}
    {B.returns.exchanges && (
      <Fragment>
        <h2>Exchanges</h2>
        <p class="prose">
          If you would rather swap than get your money back, say so when
          you email us and we will arrange it. Any design, any size, any
          frame colour — the whole range is open to you, not just the one
          you ordered. If the new one costs more you pay the difference;
          if it costs less we refund it.
        </p>
        <p class="prose">
          Everything is made to order, so an exchange is a fresh print
          rather than something taken off a shelf: expect the same
          {' '}{B.fulfilment.min_handling_days}&ndash;{B.fulfilment.dispatch_working_days}
          {' '}working days to make it and {B.fulfilment.delivery[0].min_days}&ndash;{B.fulfilment.delivery[0].max_days}
          {' '}in the post, counted from when your return reaches us. You
          have the same {B.returns.window_days} days to ask for an exchange
          as you do for a refund.
        </p>
      </Fragment>
    )}

    <h2>Damaged, faulty or wrong</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Send a photograph to <a href={`mailto:${B.email}`}>{B.email}</a>. We
      remake and resend at our cost, and you do not need to post the
      original back. If you would rather have the money, we refund in full
      including delivery.
    </p>

    <h2>Your legal rights</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Our {B.returns.window_days}-day policy is offered on top of your legal
      rights, not instead of them. Under the Consumer Contracts Regulations
      2013 you generally have 14 days to cancel an online order; prints made
      to order can be exempt from that, so we give everyone
      {' '}{B.returns.window_days} days voluntarily and do not rely on the
      exemption. Under the Consumer Rights Act 2015 you are entitled to a
      remedy if goods are faulty, and nothing here limits that.
    </p>

    <h2>What we cannot take back</h2>
    <p class="prose">
      Nothing, within the window, provided it arrives back in a condition we
      could reasonably resell — so please do not hang it with adhesive
      strips that tear the frame, and keep the glazing intact. If a returned
      print arrives damaged because it was posted loose in a bag, we will
      contact you before refunding rather than quietly reducing it.
    </p>
  </div>
</Base>
